<title>NEW ZEALAND: Energy Direct directors favour merger.</title>
<headline>Energy Direct directors favour merger.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Directors of power company EnergyDirect said in a notice to the New Zealand Stock Exchange on Tuesday that the proposed amalgamation with Wellington's Capital Power was in the company's best interests.</p>
<p>Capital Power and EnergyDirect propose to merge into a new company, TransAlta New Zealand Ltd, in which TransAlta Corp will hold a 63 percent interest. TransAlta currently holds 41 percent of EnergyDirect and all of Capital Power.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
